  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 3,
  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Number of isomeric compounds with molecular formula <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>9</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>10</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math> which</p><p>(i) do not dissolve in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>NaOH</mi></math><br />(ii) do not dissolve in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>HCl</mi></math>.</p><p>(iii) do not give orange precipitate with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></math> - DNP</p><p>(iv) on hydrogenation give identical compound with molecular formula <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>9</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>12</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math> is</p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "2",
  "solution": {
    "text": "No reaction with strong base or acid indicates presence of strong neutrality or non-reactive functional hroup with a single oxygen. No positive 2,4-DNP test indicates absence of carbonyl compound. Same compound formation upon hydrogenation indicates single double bond. Thus, it is an ether.<br /><br />As per the language of given question, the best possible isomeric structure is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Ph</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>CH</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>CH</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;(cis and trans). So, the answer is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>.",
    "image": null
  },
